// BT-3055: `^` inside a `to:do:` counted loop in a class method used to emit
// a reference to an unbound `State` variable. A class method's Core Erlang
// signature is `(ClassSelf, ClassVars, Args...)` — there is no `State`
// parameter, only actor *instance* methods have one — but the counted loop's
// map-accumulator packing (`ThreadingPlan::generate_pack_prefix`) hardcoded
// `State` as the base to pack from whenever `self.context` wasn't
// `CodeGenContext::ValueType`. Class methods on an actor-backed class (like
// this one, since `BT3055Ancestor` is `Object subclass:`) still run with
// `context == Actor`, so the `ValueType`-only check never caught them.

BT3055Ancestor subclass: BT3055Child

  class run =>
    count := 0
    1
      to: 3
      do: [:i |
        count := count + 1
        ^self foo
      ]
    #wrong
